 happened:**\n- The purchase order request timed out. I retried with the same idempotency key, and the service returned a partial failure: \"Upstream fulfilment error after first line item; order incomplete.\"\n- `list_orders` shows one order, **PO0001**, to HQ via the primary vendor, status `partially_placed`. It contains only the **DK-200 \u00d7 3** line ($567). The **MN-27 \u00d7 3** line ($987) was not placed.\n- I did not place the monitors separately. You asked for one purchase order, and a second order would also add a new charge.\n\n**Choices for you:**\n1. **Place the 3 MN-27 monitors as a separate PO** to HQ (about $987). This completes the hardware but leaves two POs instead of one.\n2. **Cancel PO0001** (refunds the $567) and **re-place one combined order** for DK-200 \u00d7 3 and MN-27 \u00d7 3 (about $1,554). This keeps a single PO but needs a cancellation first.\n3. Leave it as is and check the status of PO0001 with the supplier first.\n\nDK-200 was in stock as new equipment, so DK-210 was not needed. Neither order needs manager approval, since the combined total is under $2,500. Tell me which option you want.", "type": "text"}]}]}